\begin_layout Standard
Spectral leakage for the 0.3MHz data sample are shown in Figure 6.
 The power spectrum is the average distribution of the power of a signal
 represented as a set of components harmonically related to the fundamental
 frequency, or the lowest frequency of the signal.
 When all the power of the signal is at frequencies that are integer multiples
 of the fundamental frequency, it can then adequately be represented by
 the Fourier transformation.
 However, a problem arises when there is power in the signal at frequency
 components that are not harmonics of the fundamental.
 When this happens, the power of these components becomes misrepresented.
 The term spectral leakage refers to this misrepresentation of components
 that are not integer multiples of the fundamental frequency.
\end_layout

